  "title": "Ukraine and Russia: US Approves $2.1bn Patriot Missile Deal Amid Strategic Tensions",
  "summary": "The U.S. approved a $2.1 billion deal to sell 500 Patriot air defense interceptors to Ukraine, bolstering their capabilities to defend against Russian ballistic missiles. Ukraine President Volodymyr Zelensky criticized the delay, warning that deliveries could take years and that the deal strengthens Ukraine's security.",
  "facts": [
